  <url><loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/our-program</loc><lastmod>2026-10-15</lastmod><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-teaser.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>What are I-O faculty at Purdue really like?</video:title><video:description>A 30-second preview of the series: Franki Kung drops in on faculty and students during office hours.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/S_Pd-kZya9E</video:player_loc><video:duration>28</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-alex.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Franki Kung drops in on Alex Harris-Watson</video:title><video:description>Teams, leadership and human-AI collaboration, a new lab study of team composition, and why initiative matters in a Ph.D. applicant.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Q2crijh8LfM</video:player_loc><video:duration>201</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-brooke.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Franki Kung drops in on Brooke Macnamara</video:title><video:description>How people get better at complex skills, and why a specific research question beats a broad topic in your statement.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/HsP_KwB_pUE</video:player_loc><video:duration>181</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-franki.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Dropping in on Franki Kung</video:title><video:description>The host takes the hot seat: conflict management, humanizing workplaces in the age of AI, and how to develop a strong research question.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/VSWa_s4Mykc</video:player_loc><video:duration>217</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-louis.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Franki Kung drops in on Louis Tay</video:title><video:description>Well-being, AI and measurement, why measurement is anything but boring, and the quality that makes an applicant stand out.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/IXnz4NLox4U</video:player_loc><video:duration>167</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-sangeun.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Franki Kung drops in on Sang Eun Woo</video:title><video:description>Personality and motivation at work, what makes mentoring rewarding, and the three words that make an application stand out.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/ixjrPr1CUT8</video:player_loc><video:duration>149</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-10-15</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video><video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://www.purdueiopsych.com/images/video-emma.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Office Hours: Franki Kung drops in on Emma Showalter</video:title><video:description>A current student on the mentor program, the psychological safety in the program, and what student life is really like.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://w